Description: hw/arm/chumby_classic: Add the board's USB hub and a handoff option
 The Chumby's hub is on host 1, root hub port 2; add it ("internal-hub",
 on by default), so that port's requirements are what a guest meets.
 .
 "handoff" starts the machine as a kernel started from the running stock
 firmware does: the LCD's graphic window on and opaque with the panel
 registers read from a running Chumby, the pins as stock set them, and
 noise in RAM. The window's address is a stand-in: stock allocates it at
 run time. A window at address 0 now also blends rather than being skipped.
Author: John Merchant <john@johnmerchant.dev>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [AI generated code]
