diff --git a/docs/system/arm/chumby-classic.rst b/docs/system/arm/chumby-classic.rst
--- a/docs/system/arm/chumby-classic.rst
+++ b/docs/system/arm/chumby-classic.rst
@@ -93,6 +93,23 @@ can also be driven from QMP with ``input-send-event`` (``abs`` events on
 the ``x`` and ``y`` axes, 0 to 32767 across the screen, and the ``left``
 button). ``screendump`` captures the screen.
 
+The board's USB hub is on root hub port 2 (``internal-hub``, on by
+default), and devices given no port attach behind it, as on a Chumby.
+Transfers only reach a device if the guest has set the block up as
+hardware needs: its clocks on, the USB clock really 48 MHz, the port's
+pins multiplexed, and for port 2 USBCTRL's HOST1_TXEN_OE set and PB25-PB29
+outputs. Otherwise they end with "device not responding" (Linux's -110);
+``-d guest_errors`` says why.
+
+The clock module starts with the values of a running Chumby, whose
+oscillator is 16 MHz: a kernel whose clock tree assumes the i.MX21's usual
+26 MHz believes every rate is 1.625 times what it is, and its timers run
+slow by that much, as on a real one.
+
+``-M chumby-classic,handoff=on`` starts the machine as a kernel started
+from the running stock firmware does: the LCD's graphic window on and
+opaque, the pins of ports B, D and E as stock set them, and noise in RAM.
+
 USB devices attach to the host controller's root hub, for example a
 disk image as a USB stick and a keyboard::
 
